jsImplementationNotes:
Algorithm that exactly reproduces CPython (Objects/longobject.c _PyLong_FromUnicodeObject -> _PyUnicode_TransformDecimalAndSpaceToASCII -> PyLong_FromString):
  STEP 1 (transform, per CODE POINT, so iterate with for..of / codePointAt):
    if (cp < 127) keep the char unchanged;
    else if (isPyUnicodeSpace(cp)) replace with ' ' (0x20);
    else if (decimalValue(cp) >= 0) replace with String(decimalValue(cp));
    else replace with '?'  // guarantees later failure
  STEP 2 (parse the resulting ASCII string with base 10):
    i = 0; while (isCIsspace(t[i])) i++;                      // strip leading
    sign = 1; if (t[i]==='+'){i++} else if (t[i]==='-'){sign=-1;i++}
    // digits with PEP 515 underscores: must start with a digit, end with a digit,
    // and every '_' must be immediately preceded AND followed by a digit
    collect digits, counting only digits (not '_', not sign, not spaces)
    if (no digits) -> error
    if (digitCount > 4300) -> error   // int_max_str_digits
    j = end of digit run; while (isCIsspace(t[j])) j++;        // strip trailing
    if (j !== t.length) -> error
    return sign * BigInt(digitsWithoutUnderscores)

Implement pyRepr(s) faithfully — this is the second big source of divergence, JSON.stringify() is wrong:
  quote = "'"; if (s.includes("'") && !s.includes('"')) quote = '"';
  then per CODE POINT: if (ch === quote || ch === '\\\\') emit '\\\\'+ch;
  else if (ch === '\\n') emit '\\\\n'; else if (ch === '\\r') emit '\\\\r'; else if (ch === '\\t') emit '\\\\t';
  else if (!isPyPrintable(cp)) emit cp < 0x100 ? '\\\\x'+hex2 : cp < 0x10000 ? '\\\\u'+hex4 : '\\\\U'+hex8;   // lowercase hex, zero-padded
  else emit the char raw;
  wrap in quote. NOTE: the non-chosen quote char is NEVER escaped, and there are no \\a \\b \\f \\v \\0 escapes (VT->\\x0b, FF->\\x0c, BEL->\\x07, ESC->\\x1b).
